    ],
    "https://schema.org/articleBody": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n        \nDuo Cordelia\n\n   \nSun, Mar 7, 2027 @ 3:00 pm\nRegina, SK – @ Darke Hall\nPresented by Regina Musical Club\nBuy Tickets\n\n\n\n\nAs Duo Cordelia, violinist Vanessa Marcoux and pianist Marie-Christine Poirier invite you into an unexpected musical landscape, where classical compositions mingle with fresh repertoire, playful improvisation, and unconventional technique.\n\nBoth graduates of the Université de Montréal and individually recognized as talented musicians, the two have been curating captivating performances together for almost a decade. Their 2024 album \"Cendres\" was honoured with an Opus Award for Album of the Year in the ancient, classical, romantic, modern and postmodern category.\n\nWander with Vanessa and Marie-Christine through a program rich in storytelling and invention, where connections spark between genres that rarely intersect, and anything is possible.\n\n\n\nWatch Video:\n\nAppearances\n\n\n\n\n\nSun, Mar 7, 2027 @ 3:00 pm\n\n\nBuy Tickets\n\n\n\nRegina, SK - Darke Hall\n\nPresented by Regina Musical Club\n\n\n\n    "
      }
    ],
